      "summary": ": Today at Cardrona Aug 28, 2026 – Cardrona picked up 50cm of snow in the past 24 hours, filling in the gaps nicely heading into spring, but the mountain is working through a genuinely tricky morning because of it. Overnight warming and clear skies have set a thin crust over supersoft snow underneath, so off-piste is tough and variable everywhere right now, and conditions should soften as temperatures climb through the day. As of 11:35am, the mountain has stopped any further access due to limited terrain and capacity — patience is the name of the game today. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View and the T-Bar are running, while Captains Express, Soho Express, Willow's Quad and Wells Pipe Platter stay closed. Learners Slope and Main Basin are open for skiing, but Captains, Soho, Little Willows and Big Willows remain shut, and Ski Touring Access and Mt Cardrona are delayed while Patrol works through avalanche control — please respect all closures, they're there for your safety. Valley View terrain is ski-out only to the car park today. Gravity Cross is the one park feature running, with the rest of the terrain park closed for now. All six car parks are full, so allow extra time. The valley road is chain-free but chains should still be carried, and there's surface flooding and a slip across the road, so take it easy on the way in.",
