      "summary": ": Today at Treble Cone Friday, 28 August 2026 – Treble Cone is closed today while the mountain deals with the aftermath of this week's big storm. Multiple slips are blocking the access road, machinery is working on them now, and management is looking at using a helicopter to get around the worst of the blockages. Avalanche risk is elevated right across the terrain after a heavy dump of snow was topped with rain lower down, leaving an unstable base that needs time to settle. It's currently around 1°C up top with a westerly averaging 27km/h and gusting to 48km/h, and temperatures are set to sit below freezing through the weekend as things cool off again. None of the three lifts are turning today — Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and the Beginner Platter are all closed — and every trail is shut too, including Triple Treat, Main Street, High Street, Bullet and Saddle Track, along with the terrain zones of Home Basin, Saddle Basin, Powder Bowl, Matukituki Basin, Summit Slopes, Motatapu Chutes and Sundance. All three car parks and the access road itself are closed to traffic, so there's no way up the mountain today regardless. Friday school skiing has been cancelled, and Saturday's Snowboard Banked Slalom has been postponed to Sunday. No reopening time has been confirmed yet — crews are focused on clearing the road and reassessing the avalanche risk, so it's worth checking back before planning a trip up.",
